Joeb wrote:

> So now I'm back to healer.

> So anyway, what tips can you give me?  Should I always play Gnomes and
> head for Minetown asap to do the protection racket?

Not necessarily gnomes, but healers are great for the racket.

> When is it safe to ditch the pet, or should I keep it?  (Because I generally
> ditch them asap).

Ding ding ding! The healer class is the "petmaster" class. That's what
they're *made for*. You have a lot of ascensions for someone who
doesn't know how to use pets. Well, now it's time to learn.
The stethoscope isn't just for your enemies, and the healing spell
isn't just for yourself. Let your pets fight the bad guys instead of
risking your own HP. Every kill they get makes them stronger, and
gets rid of your enemies without making protection more expensive.

> What is a good weapon to replace the scapel with before I get
> the Staff?

Pets. Lots and lots of pets! Get a magic whistle ASAP, watch
for polymorph traps, and don't be embarrassed to use the E-word.
If you feel you really need to use a melee weapon after you've
got your protection but before you've got the Staff, a unicorn horn
is nice.

